From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 08:47:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: Select PHY configuration by TMDS clock

The PHY configuration tables are matched against the pixel clock, which
differs from the rate the PHY sees when the output format is YUV 4:2:0
(half rate) or deep color (higher rate).

Voltage level configuration depends on the actual TMDS character rate,
so match it against the TMDS clock. The MPLL and current control tables
have a column per color depth, which already accounts for the higher
rate of deep color, so keep matching them against the pixel clock, but
halve it for YUV 4:2:0. This way, for example, a 4K@60 YUV 4:2:0 mode
(594 MHz pixel clock, 297 MHz TMDS clock) picks the 297 MHz PLL
settings instead of the 594 MHz ones.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
index 1ba43472b874..55e79d18427e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -1586,11 +1586,19 @@ static int hdmi_phy_configure_dwc_hdmi_3d_tx(struct dw_hdmi *hdmi,
 		const struct dw_hdmi_plat_data *pdata,
 		unsigned long mpixelclock)
 {
+	unsigned long mtmdsclock = hdmi->hdmi_data.video_mode.mtmdsclock;
 	const struct dw_hdmi_mpll_config *mpll_config = pdata->mpll_cfg;
 	const struct dw_hdmi_curr_ctrl *curr_ctrl = pdata->cur_ctr;
 	const struct dw_hdmi_phy_config *phy_config = pdata->phy_config;
 
-	/* TOFIX Will need 420 specific PHY configuration tables */
+	/*
+	 * The MPLL and current control tables are indexed by the pixel clock
+	 * and have a column per color depth, which already accounts for the
+	 * higher TMDS rate of deep color. Only YUV 4:2:0 halves the rate
+	 * the PHY sees.
+	 */
+	if (hdmi_bus_fmt_is_yuv420(hdmi->hdmi_data.enc_out_bus_format))
+		mpixelclock /= 2;
 
 	/* PLL/MPLL Cfg - always match on final entry */
 	for (; mpll_config->mpixelclock != ~0UL; mpll_config++)
@@ -1602,7 +1610,7 @@ static int hdmi_phy_configure_dwc_hdmi_3d_tx(struct dw_hdmi *hdmi,
 			break;
 
 	for (; phy_config->mpixelclock != ~0UL; phy_config++)
-		if (mpixelclock <= phy_config->mpixelclock)
+		if (mtmdsclock <= phy_config->mpixelclock)
 			break;
 
 	if (mpll_config->mpixelclock == ~0UL ||
